cell)\n903: - Invalid action flash triggered when attempting to place cell with insufficient Flux\n904: - All animations use canvas transformations for smooth, hardware-accelerated rendering\n905: - Animation loop only runs when animations are active to preserve performance\n906: \n907: **Technical Decisions:**\n908: \n909: - Canvas-based rendering chosen over CSS animations for better performance with large grids\n910: - Easing functions: cubic-out (1 - (1-t)^3) for birth, quadratic-in (t^2) for death\n911: - Animation state tracked in React state (animations array) for reactivity\n912: - requestAnimationFrame used for smooth 60fps animation updates\n913: - Animation map (by \"row,col\" key) for efficient lookup during rendering\n914: - Separate rendering loops: one for alive cells, one for death animations\n915: - Invalid action flash uses setTimeout (200ms) for simple fade-out effect\n916: - All timing uses window.performance.now() for accurate delta calculation\n917: \n918: **Test Coverage:**\n919: \n920: - All existing 326 tests continue to pass\n921: - Integration verified through manual testing\n922: - Performance confirmed to maintain 60fps with active animations\n923: \n924: **Completed**: Sprint 4.2 Cell Animations (2026-02-16) - Birth, death, and invalid action animations implemented\n925: \n926: **Dependencies**: Canvas rendering, UI components\n927: \n928: ### 4.3 Mobile Enhancements (MEDIUM - Mobile Experience)\n929: \n930: - [x] Implement touch-action handling\n931:   - touch-action: none on canvas element\n932:   - PreventDefault on all touch events\n933:   - Stop scroll and zoom during interaction\n934:   - Already implemented in CanvasGrid.tsx (line 211)\n935: - [x] Implement minimum touch targets\n936:   - Ensure all buttons ≥44×44px\n937:   - Spacious clickable areas\n938:   - Already implemented in GlassHUD.css (lines 195-196)\n939: - [ ] Implement touch ripple effect (optional)\n940:   - Visual feedback on touch\n941:   - Radial ripple animation\n942: - [ ] Implement mobile expert settings access\n943:   - Triple-tap top-left corner gesture\n944:   - Confirm gesture doesn't conflict with game controls\n945: \n946: **Dependencies**: User interaction, UI components\n947: \n948: ---\n949: \n950: ## Sprint 5: Expert Settings & Advanced Features\n951: \n952: _Goal: Advanced tuning, customization, and power features_\n953: \n954: ### 5.1 Expert Settings Panel (MEDIUM - Tuning)\n955: \n956: - [ ] Implement expert settings panel (src/components/ExpertSettings.tsx)\n957:   - Access via keyboard shortcut (`), Settings menu, or mobile gesture\n958:   - Modal overlay or sidebar\n959:   - Collapsible sections by category\n960: - [ ] Implement movement detection parameters\n961:   - Centroid history length (3-10, default 5)\n962:   - Movement threshold (0.1-2.0, default 0.5)\n963:   - Minimum cluster size (1-5, default 1)\n964: - [ ] Implement scoring parameters\n965:   - Mover points per generation (1-100, default 10)\n966:   - Oscillator points per generation (0-20, default 2)\n967:   - Score multiplier (0.1-5.0, default 1.0)\n968: - [ ] Implement level generation parameters\n969:   - Base time seconds (10-120, default 45)\n970:   - Time increment per level (0-60, default 15)\n971:   - Base Flux (5-50, default 20)\n972:   - Difficulty scaling mode: TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME\n973: - [ ] Implement grid sizing parameters\n974:   - Mobile cell size (14-24, default 18)\n975:   - Desktop cell size (16-28, default 20)\n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 975)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"  - Brief pulse/flash on point gain\n  - Milestone flash every 100 points\n  - Already implemented in ScoreDisplay.tsx\n- [ ] Implement Flux counter animation\n  - Smooth transitions when values change\n  - Color coding transitions (green → yellow → orange → red)\n  - Color coding implemented, transitions not yet added\n- [x] Implement intro glitch effect\